// A variadic parameter has to name its element type.

// `T` is what the collected list holds, and nothing else says what that is.
// With no annotation the back end picks the integer array, so `firstf(1.5, 2.5)`
// pushed two doubles into an `IntArr` and read back `1.0`. A silently wrong
// answer, from a program that compiled clean.

firstf(...rest) -> float => rest.get(0)

main() -> int {
    info("{firstf(1.5, 2.5)}")
    0
}
